# 🥇 Gold Layer

## Overview

The Gold layer represents the business intelligence and analytical stage of the Financial Audit Trail & Fraud Detection pipeline. Building upon the validated and enriched transaction records produced by the Silver layer, it aggregates financial data into business-oriented datasets optimized for reporting, dashboarding, and operational monitoring.

Rather than focusing on individual transaction records, the Gold layer transforms detailed financial events into meaningful business metrics that provide insights into customer activity, fraud distribution, transaction trends, and overall financial health. These aggregated datasets enable financial analysts, auditors, and decision-makers to monitor operational performance while identifying potential risks and unusual transaction patterns.

To support multiple analytical perspectives, the Gold layer generates dedicated summary tables for user-level transaction behavior, fraud distribution analysis, and daily financial KPIs. These data marts serve as the foundation for interactive dashboards, audit reporting, and executive-level business intelligence.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

* Aggregate validated financial transactions into business-ready analytical datasets.
* Generate user-level transaction summaries for customer activity analysis.
* Produce fraud distribution metrics for monitoring suspicious financial behavior.
* Calculate daily operational KPIs for executive reporting and dashboard visualization.
* Simplify complex transactional data into decision-ready business metrics.
* Provide optimized data marts for downstream business intelligence and audit analytics.

